meta {
  name: Handshake Cluster
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/clusters/{{clusterId}}/handshake
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{joinTokenJwt}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "agent_version": "0.1.0",
    "csr": "-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE REQUEST-----\n<base64-encoded PKCS#10 CSR>\n-----END CERTIFICATE REQUEST-----"
  }
}

docs {
  One-time bootstrap call made by the sAId-Kick agent immediately after the helm installer runs.
  Verifies the HS256 join-token, signs the agent's CSR via Vault PKI, and transitions the
  cluster to state ready.

  Auth:
    Authorization: Bearer <join_token_jwt>  (issued by POST /clusters, 1-hour TTL, single-use)

  Request body:
    agent_version  string — semver of the installed agent (stored for observability)
    csr            string — PEM-encoded PKCS#10 certificate signing request

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Extract Bearer token from Authorization header — 401 if missing or malformed.
    2. Verify HS256 signature and expiry; extract sub (cluster ID) and jti — 401 if invalid or expired.
    3. Confirm token subject matches the :id path param — 401 if mismatch.
    4. Load cluster row — 404 if not found.
    5. Reject if cluster state is decommissioned — 410 gone.
    6. Bind and validate request body; csr field required — 422 if missing.
    7. PEM-decode and x509-parse the CSR — 422 if not a valid PKCS#10 block.
    8. Call Vault PKI SignCSR (CN = saidkick-agent-<id>, TTL = 90 days) — 503 if PKI not configured.
    9. In one transaction: insert JTI into used_join_tokens (unique constraint burns it) — 410 if already used;
       update cluster row (state=ready, agent_version, agent_cert_serial, registered_at, last_heartbeat_at).
    10. Write cluster.agent_bootstrapped to audit_logs (best effort, outside transaction).

  Responses:
    200 OK                        — { client_cert_pem, ca_pem, hub_endpoint }
    401 unauthorized              — missing, malformed, or expired join token; or token targets wrong cluster
    404 not_found                 — cluster not found
    410 gone                      — cluster decommissioned, or join token already used
    422 validation_failed         — csr missing or not a valid PEM PKCS#10 certificate request
    503 vault_pki_not_configured  — VAULT_PKI_MOUNT / VAULT_PKI_ROLE env vars not set
}
